# Daybreak: statistics you can read.
#
# Fifty-three methods, each returning the same shaped record, each described
# twice: once for a reader who knows what a confidence interval is and once for
# a reader who does not. The two readings come from the same numbers and are
# generated by deterministic R code. No language model writes or alters a
# value anywhere in this application.
#
# The file layout follows the path a result takes. catalog.R describes the
# methods as data. data_io.R reads files. The three engine files compute.
# reporting.R and explanations.R write the two readings. plots.R draws.
# exports.R packages. ui_helpers.R and this file put it on screen.
# Copyright Abhik Roy. PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0.

# RStudio's Run App button opens this file directly, so the dependency check
# belongs here as well as in the Finder launcher.
if (!isTRUE(getOption("daybreak.dependencies.checked"))) {
  source("install.R", chdir = TRUE)
}

options(shiny.maxRequestSize = 200 * 1024^2)

